  "section_notes": "The S2 final text sets no numeric failure-rate cap and no sales stop, so a 6.2% model like Northwind's Hearth 10 is not barred, while per-model rates go to purchasers but not the public. S5 converts the 8/100k per-model rate into a review and public-explanation trigger rather than a mandatory recall, leaving corrective action open-ended, which favours Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S1's 24-hour reporting and S4's 36-month suppression deadline are the strongest protections in the text; S3's 72-month retrofit deadline sits within Northwind's 6-year red line."
